WEBVTT

00:00:00.515 --> 00:00:03.087
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1.

00:00:03.147 --> 00:00:07.000
A Ghost in Love and Other Plays by Michael Dean.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:13.064
Published and Copyright Oxford University Press, 2007.

00:00:13.124 --> 00:00:17.808
One Ghost for the Day, One Ghost for the Night.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:38.746
Performed by Ben Elliott, Lawrence Kennedy, Sara Martland, Coraline Sheldon, and Terry Wilton.

00:00:38.806 --> 00:00:53.530
One ghost for the day, one ghost for the night.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:58.826
Scene one, a ghost comes to Richard Little.

00:00:58.886 --> 00:01:01.223
The year is 1653.

00:01:01.283 --> 00:01:10.890
It is a cold, dark winter night, and Richard Little, a man of forty, is sitting in his chair.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.060
He is reading a book.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.142
He hears something.

00:01:15.202 --> 00:01:21.176
He goes to the window, looks out, and then goes back to the chair.

00:01:21.236 --> 00:01:23.908
His wife Mary comes in.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.149
She is making a dress.

00:01:26.209 --> 00:01:30.181
She has the dress in her hand.

00:01:30.241 --> 00:01:36.084
Mary, I can hear something outside.

00:01:36.144 --> 00:01:38.346
There's nothing there.

00:01:38.406 --> 00:01:40.928
Read your book, Richard.

00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:43.199
Come and sit with me.

00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:46.030
No, I'm making a dress.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.372
I'm going upstairs.

00:01:48.432 --> 00:01:50.293
Mary, please.

00:01:50.353 --> 00:01:52.604
There's something out there.

00:01:52.664 --> 00:01:54.025
Oh, Richard.

00:01:54.045 --> 00:01:59.188
Hello, Richard.

00:01:59.248 --> 00:02:00.564
Ah!

00:02:00.624 --> 00:02:02.328
You!

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.321
James!

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.553
James Heston!

00:02:06.612 --> 00:02:08.254
But you...

00:02:08.314 --> 00:02:09.765
You are dead!

00:02:09.825 --> 00:02:10.846
Yes.

00:02:10.905 --> 00:02:12.457
I am dead.

00:02:12.517 --> 00:02:15.740
But I can't find peace because of you.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.742
Because of me?

00:02:17.802 --> 00:02:18.852
Why?

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.715
Why because of me?

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.917
Beth had a new husband after me.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.609
That animal!

00:02:26.668 --> 00:02:27.700
Cage!

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.090
Yes.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.254
Beth was a good woman.

00:02:31.314 --> 00:02:33.356
and a good sister to me.

00:02:33.416 --> 00:02:36.438
I said to her, don't go with Keach.

00:02:36.498 --> 00:02:38.178
Think of James.

00:02:38.238 --> 00:02:39.960
He's dead now.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:44.382
She was Keach's wife for only three months.

00:02:44.442 --> 00:02:46.403
Then she died.

00:02:46.463 --> 00:02:49.734
And now Keach has my son.

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:53.026
And he has my son's money.

00:02:53.086 --> 00:02:56.828
Ah, I understand now.

00:02:56.888 --> 00:02:59.851
Oh, you remember now?

00:02:59.911 --> 00:03:09.816
Before I died, I said to you, my boy gets my money at 21, and not before.

00:03:09.876 --> 00:03:12.146
He is eight now.

00:03:12.206 --> 00:03:13.387
Eight.

00:03:13.447 --> 00:03:16.508
And Keach has his money.

00:03:16.568 --> 00:03:18.829
I'm sorry about that.

00:03:18.889 --> 00:03:20.830
But what can I do?

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:24.251
You must get my boy's money.

00:03:24.311 --> 00:03:26.152
Get it from Keach.

00:03:26.212 --> 00:03:27.302
No.

00:03:27.362 --> 00:03:30.008
Keach can kill me with one hand.

00:03:30.068 --> 00:03:31.224
He's big.

00:03:31.284 --> 00:03:33.936
He always has a knife in his pocket.

00:03:33.996 --> 00:03:37.538
Last year, he killed a man with that knife.

00:03:37.598 --> 00:03:40.200
I'm afraid of him, James.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.202
Are you afraid of me?

00:03:42.262 --> 00:03:43.192
No.

00:03:43.252 --> 00:03:44.534
Oh.

00:03:44.594 --> 00:03:46.495
Yes, a little.

00:03:46.555 --> 00:03:48.246
You're a ghost.

00:03:48.306 --> 00:03:50.658
Only a little, eh?

00:03:50.718 --> 00:03:52.940
Look at the table.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.441
Oh, no.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.772
The table is moving.

00:03:56.832 --> 00:03:57.904
Oh, no.

00:03:57.924 --> 00:03:59.194
Oh.

00:03:59.254 --> 00:04:02.676
The chair is moving now.

00:04:02.736 --> 00:04:05.678
And now my chair is moving.

00:04:05.738 --> 00:04:09.862
James, don't do this to me.

00:04:09.922 --> 00:04:18.819
At this minute, Keach is building a new home in a village near here with my son's money.

00:04:18.878 --> 00:04:20.540
Stop him.

00:04:20.599 --> 00:04:22.742
I'm sorry, James.

00:04:22.802 --> 00:04:25.443
I can't.

00:04:25.503 --> 00:04:28.540
I didn't want.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:35.718
That was my hand, but James, can you get in my head?

00:04:35.778 --> 00:04:39.080
Can you tell my hand?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:05:02.648
Yes, Richard, and your answer is going to be yes, or you are going to do this again and again and again and I'm going mad.

00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:07.290
Why do my hands throw a book when I don't want to?

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:11.311
Can all dead people do this?

00:05:11.371 --> 00:05:16.823
Can they get into a man's head so he moves a chair or throws a book?

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.644
Oh, yes.

00:05:18.703 --> 00:05:29.078
Now, I can do it to you again, or you can say yes and get my son's money, which?

00:05:29.138 --> 00:05:30.968
But how?

00:05:31.028 --> 00:05:34.391
How can I get the money from Keach?

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.022
Sit down.

00:05:36.082 --> 00:05:39.634
I'm going to tell you.

00:05:39.694 --> 00:05:42.597
Scene two.

00:05:42.657 --> 00:05:45.340
David Keach in court.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:54.316
In the court we can see Judge Timbs, Keach, Barker, Reynolds, Richard and Mary.

00:05:54.376 --> 00:05:58.632
There are six women and six men behind Keach.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:02.756
They are from the village and they are watching the trial.

00:06:02.816 --> 00:06:08.530
Judge Timbs is in a big chair in front of the court.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:18.266
My name is Oliver Barker and I speak for Richard Little here today.

00:06:18.326 --> 00:06:23.720
Judge Timbs, I speak for David Keach here today.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.195
My name is Philip Reynolds.

00:06:26.255 --> 00:06:28.599
That Keach took the boy's money.

00:06:28.659 --> 00:06:30.709
You can see it in his face.

00:06:30.769 --> 00:06:31.940
Oh, Lil.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.321
We must listen to Oliver Barker and Philip Reynolds first.

00:06:36.381 --> 00:06:38.982
Keach is the boy Tom's father now.

00:06:39.002 --> 00:06:45.264
A good father doesn't take his son's money and build a new house with it.

00:06:45.324 --> 00:06:47.495
Be quiet in my court.

00:06:47.555 --> 00:06:48.875
Sorry.

00:06:48.935 --> 00:06:50.696
Oliver Barker.

00:06:50.756 --> 00:06:52.576
You can begin.

00:06:52.636 --> 00:06:54.715
Judge Timbs.

00:06:54.775 --> 00:07:00.515
Before James Heston died, he said this to Richard Little.

00:07:00.575 --> 00:07:06.267
He said, my boy gets my money at 21 and not before.

00:07:06.327 --> 00:07:10.228
At 21 and not before.

00:07:10.288 --> 00:07:12.108
Yes, Judge.

00:07:12.168 --> 00:07:15.580
But Keach has this money now.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.400
The boy's money.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:20.582
He is building a big house with it.

00:07:20.642 --> 00:07:22.632
We all know that.

00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:25.098
Put Keach in prison, I say.

00:07:25.157 --> 00:07:26.083
Hmm.

00:07:26.142 --> 00:07:27.504
Five years.

00:07:27.564 --> 00:07:28.364
No.

00:07:28.424 --> 00:07:29.335
Ten.

00:07:29.395 --> 00:07:30.286
You.

00:07:30.345 --> 00:07:32.738
Don't eat in my court.

00:07:32.798 --> 00:07:34.699
Philip Reynolds.

00:07:34.759 --> 00:07:36.030
Speak.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.812
Judge Timbs.

00:07:37.871 --> 00:07:40.914
Yes, there is a house in a village near here.

00:07:40.974 --> 00:07:43.346
And yes, it is Keach's house.

00:07:43.406 --> 00:07:47.698
But the money for it is not young Tom's money.

00:07:47.758 --> 00:07:50.421
Not Tom's money.

00:07:50.441 --> 00:07:52.682
No, Judge Timbs.

00:07:52.742 --> 00:07:55.473
It is David Keach's money.

00:07:55.533 --> 00:08:02.466
So one day Keach is not rich and the next day he is rich.

00:08:02.526 --> 00:08:05.888
He has money for a house.

00:08:05.948 --> 00:08:10.290
Call David Keach.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:12.712
David Keach.

00:08:12.772 --> 00:08:15.494
Where is the boy Tom's money?

00:08:15.554 --> 00:08:17.445
Do you have it at home?

00:08:17.505 --> 00:08:18.656
No.

00:08:18.715 --> 00:08:20.547
Keach took the money.

00:08:20.607 --> 00:08:21.908
It was Keach.

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:23.739
I said Keach took the money.

00:08:23.799 --> 00:08:25.822
I said that yesterday.

00:08:25.882 --> 00:08:28.996
I have the money here, in this court.

00:08:29.056 --> 00:08:30.957
The money here?

00:08:31.017 --> 00:08:32.568
Teaching them what in this court?

00:08:32.628 --> 00:08:33.099
Never.

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:34.029
In this court?

00:08:34.049 --> 00:08:35.490
Never.

00:08:35.551 --> 00:08:38.132
The money is under my chair.

00:08:38.192 --> 00:08:39.373
You, woman.

00:08:39.433 --> 00:08:40.904
Bring me the money.

00:08:40.964 --> 00:08:42.025
Me?

00:08:42.085 --> 00:08:44.186
Yes, you.

00:08:44.246 --> 00:08:46.839
Here you are.

00:08:46.898 --> 00:08:48.480
Here.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.350
Judge Timbs.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.522
Here.

00:08:51.582 --> 00:08:52.992
Richard Little.

00:08:53.052 --> 00:08:54.103
Here.

00:08:54.163 --> 00:08:55.572
Look, everybody.

00:08:55.632 --> 00:08:57.401
Here is the money.

00:08:57.461 --> 00:08:59.952
So I didn't take it from the boy.

00:09:00.012 --> 00:09:01.904
You hear me, Richard Little?

00:09:01.964 --> 00:09:03.354
Yes.

00:09:03.414 --> 00:09:04.976
One minute.

00:09:05.036 --> 00:09:06.896
Richard Little.

00:09:06.956 --> 00:09:09.458
Yes, Judge Timbs?

00:09:09.518 --> 00:09:13.571
You said, Keach took the boy's money.

00:09:13.631 --> 00:09:14.992
You said that.

00:09:15.052 --> 00:09:15.752
Why?

00:09:15.772 --> 00:09:17.734
Why man?

00:09:17.794 --> 00:09:18.774
Why?

00:09:18.794 --> 00:09:22.236
Why say that?

00:09:22.296 --> 00:09:24.108
Because...

00:09:24.168 --> 00:09:25.850
Because...

00:09:25.911 --> 00:09:28.744
Because James Heston came to my home.

00:09:28.764 --> 00:09:29.965
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:29.985 --> 00:09:31.526
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:31.546 --> 00:09:32.587
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:32.607 --> 00:09:33.167
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:33.187 --> 00:09:33.767
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:33.787 --> 00:09:34.328
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:34.348 --> 00:09:34.888
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:35.728
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:35.748 --> 00:09:36.429
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:36.449 --> 00:09:37.269
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:37.329 --> 00:09:38.810
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.441
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:40.501 --> 00:09:42.032
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:42.052 --> 00:09:42.972
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:42.992 --> 00:09:44.073
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:44.093 --> 00:09:44.914
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:45.514
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:45.534 --> 00:09:46.154
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:46.174 --> 00:09:46.755
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:46.775 --> 00:09:47.395
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:47.415 --> 00:09:48.015
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:48.035 --> 00:09:49.356
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:49.376 --> 00:09:51.117
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:51.137 --> 00:09:52.818
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:52.838 --> 00:09:54.059
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:54.099 --> 00:09:55.320
James Heston said it to me.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:10:00.062
James Heston said it to me Can I take him home now, please?

00:10:00.122 --> 00:10:02.654
I am not ill.

00:10:02.714 --> 00:10:04.044
Stop laughing.

00:10:04.104 --> 00:10:06.026
Be quiet, all of you.

00:10:06.086 --> 00:10:08.558
Sit down, Mary.

00:10:08.618 --> 00:10:10.818
Thank you.

00:10:10.878 --> 00:10:13.620
Yes, James Heston is dead.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.562
And yes, James Heston spoke to me.

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:20.134
I want James Heston here.

00:10:20.194 --> 00:10:24.567
Now, he can tell you he is ill.

00:10:24.627 --> 00:10:25.763
He's mad.

00:10:25.823 --> 00:10:27.529
Let's listen to him.

00:10:27.589 --> 00:10:29.640
Yes, we can listen to him.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:31.072
Be quiet.

00:10:31.132 --> 00:10:33.503
Call James Heston.

00:10:33.563 --> 00:10:37.476
I say, call James Heston to this court.

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:39.868
Heston is a dead man.

00:10:39.928 --> 00:10:42.299
And Richard Little is mad.

00:10:42.359 --> 00:10:46.692
Call James Heston.

00:10:46.752 --> 00:10:50.975
I am James Heston.

00:10:51.035 --> 00:10:52.656
No!

00:10:52.716 --> 00:10:54.555
No!

00:10:54.616 --> 00:10:57.065
No!

00:10:57.126 --> 00:10:59.187
Oh, please, no!

00:10:59.247 --> 00:11:01.138
It's Heston!

00:11:01.198 --> 00:11:01.868
Ow!

00:11:01.928 --> 00:11:03.459
Oh, my friend!

00:11:03.519 --> 00:11:04.800
Oh, oh, Heston!

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:05.601
Heston, dead?

00:11:05.661 --> 00:11:09.092
James Heston, is it you?

00:11:09.152 --> 00:11:12.124
Did you speak to Richard Little?

00:11:12.184 --> 00:11:13.766
Yes.

00:11:13.826 --> 00:11:15.707
What did you say?

00:11:15.727 --> 00:11:26.406
I told him, Keach took my boy's money, and then Keach killed a man in the next village.

00:11:26.466 --> 00:11:28.810
He was a rich man.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.152
Keach took his money.

00:11:31.212 --> 00:11:33.484
You see the money now?

00:11:33.544 --> 00:11:36.956
Here, in this court.

00:11:37.016 --> 00:11:40.158
I can't kill Heston.

00:11:40.218 --> 00:11:41.950
Heston is dead.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:45.242
But you, you, Richard Little.

00:11:45.302 --> 00:11:47.734
You brought me to this court.

00:11:47.794 --> 00:11:50.788
I'm going to kill you next.

00:11:50.848 --> 00:11:52.548
Stop him!

00:11:52.608 --> 00:11:54.120
Stop him!

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:56.046
It was Keach!

00:11:56.106 --> 00:11:58.091
Keach took the money!

00:11:58.151 --> 00:11:59.402
I said that!

00:11:59.462 --> 00:12:01.554
I said Keach took the money!

00:12:01.614 --> 00:12:04.456
This court says Keach took the money!

00:12:04.476 --> 00:12:06.678
And Keach killed the man!

00:12:06.698 --> 00:12:12.412
Now find David Keach and bring him to me!

00:12:12.473 --> 00:12:15.544
Scene three.

00:12:15.604 --> 00:12:18.537
Keach finds Richard Little.

00:12:18.597 --> 00:12:23.221
Richard is sitting in his chair at home.

00:12:23.281 --> 00:12:25.647
What's that?

00:12:25.708 --> 00:12:28.334
Can I hear something?

00:12:28.394 --> 00:12:30.294
Mary?

00:12:30.354 --> 00:12:31.465
Is that you?

00:12:31.485 --> 00:12:34.126
Oh, no.

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:36.197
It's not James again.

00:12:36.257 --> 00:12:38.768
James, is that you?

00:12:38.788 --> 00:12:43.770
Oh, no.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:46.681
Oh, no.

00:12:46.741 --> 00:12:49.172
Keach, please.

00:12:49.232 --> 00:12:50.152
No.

00:12:50.172 --> 00:12:53.404
Oh, no.

00:12:53.464 --> 00:12:55.308
Not Richard.

00:12:55.368 --> 00:12:59.444
Not my darling, darling Richard.

00:12:59.504 --> 00:13:02.156
Keach killed him.

00:13:02.216 --> 00:13:08.591
You're going to go to prison for this, Keach.

00:13:08.651 --> 00:13:15.876
Scene four, a visit for Keach in prison.

00:13:15.935 --> 00:13:18.198
Keach is in prison.

00:13:18.258 --> 00:13:20.429
He is sitting on his bed.

00:13:20.489 --> 00:13:26.692
He has a table, a chair, and a book there, too.

00:13:26.752 --> 00:13:29.583
Hello?

00:13:29.643 --> 00:13:31.233
What's that?

00:13:31.294 --> 00:13:34.044
Is there someone there?

00:13:34.104 --> 00:13:35.334
Ah!

00:13:35.394 --> 00:13:36.864
My table!

00:13:36.924 --> 00:13:39.565
My table is moving!

00:13:39.625 --> 00:13:40.895
Ah!

00:13:40.955 --> 00:13:43.196
Now the bed's moving!

00:13:43.256 --> 00:13:45.416
Am I ill?

00:13:45.476 --> 00:13:48.437
Oh my head!

00:13:48.497 --> 00:13:50.177
Oh!

00:13:50.237 --> 00:13:53.258
Now the chair is moving!

00:13:53.318 --> 00:13:56.413
What's happening?

00:13:56.473 --> 00:14:00.010
Why did I do that?

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.182
Am I mad?

00:14:02.242 --> 00:14:07.135
It was my hand, but...

00:14:07.195 --> 00:14:08.976
You're dead.

00:14:09.036 --> 00:14:10.698
I killed you.

00:14:10.758 --> 00:14:12.008
Yes.

00:14:12.068 --> 00:14:13.500
I'm dead.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.442
And you killed me.

00:14:15.502 --> 00:14:17.953
But I'm not going away.

00:14:18.013 --> 00:14:22.326
I'm staying here in prison with you.

00:14:22.386 --> 00:14:25.188
You can't hit me now.

00:14:25.248 --> 00:14:27.456
You can't hit a ghost.

00:14:27.516 --> 00:14:30.394
And you can't kill me again.

00:14:30.454 --> 00:14:32.504
But we can talk.

00:14:32.564 --> 00:14:35.066
We have time for that.

00:14:35.126 --> 00:14:38.238
We have all day.

00:14:38.298 --> 00:14:42.470
And you can do that all day too.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.332
All day?

00:14:44.392 --> 00:14:45.812
All the time?

00:14:45.872 --> 00:14:47.514
Yes.

00:14:47.574 --> 00:14:50.605
Now throw the book across the room again.

00:14:50.625 --> 00:14:52.366
And again.

00:14:52.386 --> 00:14:54.835
And again.

00:14:54.895 --> 00:14:58.354
And again!

00:14:58.414 --> 00:14:59.495
Oh no!

00:14:59.555 --> 00:15:00.506
Please!

00:15:00.526 --> 00:15:04.367
Are all my days going to be like this?

00:15:04.427 --> 00:15:06.708
Your days, yes.

00:15:06.768 --> 00:15:11.680
And for your nights, I have a friend here.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.752
Hello Richard.

00:15:13.812 --> 00:15:15.322
Hello David.

00:15:15.382 --> 00:15:16.412
You?

00:15:16.472 --> 00:15:18.284
You here too?

00:15:18.344 --> 00:15:19.944
Yes.

00:15:20.004 --> 00:15:24.796
David, throw the book across the room please.

00:15:24.856 --> 00:15:26.894
Thank you.

00:15:26.954 --> 00:15:30.382
I'm going to be here at night, David.

00:15:30.442 --> 00:15:33.896
And you have Richard here every day.

00:15:33.956 --> 00:15:35.137
All right?

00:15:35.197 --> 00:15:37.980
Oh, no.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:38.410
No!

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:41.032
One ghost for the day.

00:15:41.092 --> 00:15:43.484
One ghost for the night.

00:15:43.544 --> 00:15:52.160
Now, throw the book across the room again.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:16:15.066
Sleep Now, My Darling, performed by Ben Cowan, Candida Gabbins, Fiona Molison, Vince Nichols, and Chris Rowe.

00:16:15.126 --> 00:16:26.946
Sleep Now, My Darling. Scene one.

00:16:27.007 --> 00:16:29.234
Jenny must stay at home.

00:16:29.294 --> 00:16:31.586
It is a hot summer day.

00:16:31.646 --> 00:16:35.890
Jenny and Gilbert Lawson are having breakfast at a table in their garden.

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:39.032
Gilbert is reading a book.

00:16:39.092 --> 00:16:44.336
Gilbert, can I come with you to America?

00:16:44.396 --> 00:16:45.556
What?

00:16:45.616 --> 00:16:49.139
Oh, Gilbert, please listen to me.

00:16:49.199 --> 00:16:53.342
I said, can I come to America too?

00:16:53.402 --> 00:16:55.901
This is good bread.

00:16:55.961 --> 00:16:57.018
Did you make it?

00:16:57.078 --> 00:16:57.928
Yes.

00:16:57.988 --> 00:17:02.530
Gilbert, I said, can I come with you?

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.281
No, Jenny.

00:17:04.341 --> 00:17:06.481
You have work here.

00:17:06.542 --> 00:17:10.352
There's the house, the garden.

00:17:10.412 --> 00:17:13.814
I remember My New Friend.

00:17:13.874 --> 00:17:16.195
It was your best film.

00:17:16.255 --> 00:17:18.846
It was my best film, too.

00:17:18.906 --> 00:17:21.126
They were happy days.

00:17:21.186 --> 00:17:22.547
Yes.

00:17:22.607 --> 00:17:25.740
I watched my new friend again last week.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:28.695
It's the best Gilbert Lawson film.

00:17:28.755 --> 00:17:31.116
And you were good in it, my love.

00:17:31.176 --> 00:17:33.138
You're a good actress.

00:17:33.198 --> 00:17:36.150
The film had a good director.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:38.181
Gilbert Lawson.

00:17:38.241 --> 00:17:39.952
Oh, thank you.

00:17:40.012 --> 00:17:42.794
But now I have this new film.

00:17:42.854 --> 00:17:46.176
So I must go to America for six weeks.

00:17:46.236 --> 00:17:49.799
Gilbert, can I be in this film, too?

00:17:49.859 --> 00:17:52.441
I want to be an actress again.

00:17:52.501 --> 00:17:54.562
Perhaps next time.

00:17:54.622 --> 00:17:55.984
Would you like that?

00:17:56.044 --> 00:17:58.756
Perhaps you can be in the next film.

00:17:58.816 --> 00:18:00.896
You said that before.

00:18:00.956 --> 00:18:02.307
Did I?

00:18:02.367 --> 00:18:03.707
Yes.

00:18:03.767 --> 00:18:06.358
This bread is very good.

00:18:06.418 --> 00:18:09.199
Can we go to America together then?

00:18:09.259 --> 00:18:10.860
Not for a film.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.470
Just you and me.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.491
Perhaps next year.

00:18:14.551 --> 00:18:16.051
Perhaps.

00:18:16.111 --> 00:18:18.112
Next year then?

00:18:18.172 --> 00:18:19.342
Yes.

00:18:19.402 --> 00:18:20.953
Next year.

00:18:21.013 --> 00:18:23.183
Love I must go now.

00:18:23.243 --> 00:18:25.582
I'm going to be late for the plane.

00:18:25.642 --> 00:18:27.530
I love you, Jenny.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:31.852
I love you too, darling.

00:18:31.912 --> 00:18:34.782
Scene two.

00:18:34.842 --> 00:18:37.623
Jenny talks to a film student.

00:18:37.683 --> 00:18:39.873
It is six weeks later.

00:18:39.933 --> 00:18:42.524
Jenny is having a coffee at the airport.

00:18:42.584 --> 00:18:45.094
She is waiting for Gilbert's plane.

00:18:45.154 --> 00:18:47.695
A young man, Henry, sees her.

00:18:47.755 --> 00:18:51.026
Henry has a big bag in his hand.

00:18:51.086 --> 00:18:52.876
Hello?

00:18:52.936 --> 00:18:55.464
Are you Jenny Lawson?

00:18:55.524 --> 00:18:58.472
Yes, I knew it.

00:18:58.532 --> 00:19:00.554
Here you are.

00:19:00.614 --> 00:19:03.304
And do you want something?

00:19:03.365 --> 00:19:04.995
Thanks.

00:19:05.055 --> 00:19:07.766
Sorry, but do I know you?

00:19:07.827 --> 00:19:09.527
A Coke for me, please.

00:19:09.587 --> 00:19:10.738
And a sandwich.

00:19:10.798 --> 00:19:13.359
One Coke, one sandwich.

00:19:13.419 --> 00:19:15.090
Oh, sorry.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.321
Yes, I know your film.

00:19:17.381 --> 00:19:19.212
My New Friend.

00:19:19.272 --> 00:19:20.992
And I know Gilbert.

00:19:21.052 --> 00:19:22.524
Can I sit down?

00:19:22.584 --> 00:19:26.266
You can't stand up and have a Coke and a sandwich.

00:19:26.326 --> 00:19:28.087
Wait a minute.

00:19:28.148 --> 00:19:29.708
I know you.

00:19:29.768 --> 00:19:31.379
I know your face.

00:19:31.439 --> 00:19:33.791
But I can't remember.

00:19:33.851 --> 00:19:37.433
Tell me, how do you know Gilbert?

00:19:37.493 --> 00:19:40.295
I'm learning about his work.

00:19:40.355 --> 00:19:43.206
I know all the Gilbert Lawson films.

00:19:43.266 --> 00:19:45.698
But forget about me.

00:19:45.758 --> 00:19:48.160
I want to talk about you.

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.851
You aren't happy.

00:19:49.911 --> 00:19:51.052
I can see that.

00:19:51.112 --> 00:19:51.936
What?

00:19:51.996 --> 00:19:56.301
You can't say that!

00:19:56.361 --> 00:20:00.663
A Coke and a sandwich.

00:20:00.723 --> 00:20:01.503
Thank you.

00:20:01.563 --> 00:20:02.924
That's okay.

00:20:02.984 --> 00:20:04.734
Sandwich is very good.

00:20:04.754 --> 00:20:08.176
I had them for lunch sometimes.

00:20:08.236 --> 00:20:10.626
Yes, you're right.

00:20:10.686 --> 00:20:11.537
It's very good.

00:20:11.597 --> 00:20:12.157
Thank you.

00:20:12.217 --> 00:20:13.478
That's okay.

00:20:13.538 --> 00:20:14.558
Goodbye then.

00:20:14.578 --> 00:20:18.389
I must go soon.

00:20:18.449 --> 00:20:20.200
What do you do every day?

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.183
What?

00:20:21.243 --> 00:20:22.956
I don't know you.

00:20:23.016 --> 00:20:24.287
You can't ask.

00:20:24.347 --> 00:20:24.827
Jenny.

00:20:24.887 --> 00:20:25.787
Please.

00:20:25.847 --> 00:20:26.768
Tell me.

00:20:26.828 --> 00:20:29.638
What do you do every day?

00:20:29.698 --> 00:20:31.959
Okay.

00:20:32.019 --> 00:20:33.670
Here's your answer.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:36.790
I get up in the morning and then I do nothing.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.441
We have no children.

00:20:38.501 --> 00:20:40.231
A woman does the house for me.

00:20:40.291 --> 00:20:42.202
A man does the garden.

00:20:42.262 --> 00:20:43.662
Do you have friends?

00:20:43.722 --> 00:20:44.513
Yes.

00:20:44.573 --> 00:20:45.842
No.

00:20:45.902 --> 00:20:48.362
I have coffee with people.

00:20:48.422 --> 00:20:50.283
I have dinner with people.

00:20:50.343 --> 00:20:56.064
We say things like nice weather for the time of year, but we don't talk.

00:20:56.124 --> 00:20:58.594
Yes, I understand.

00:20:58.654 --> 00:21:01.675
Now I'm going to tell you about me.

00:21:01.735 --> 00:21:03.085
I'm 20.

00:21:03.145 --> 00:21:05.265
I go to America sometimes.

00:21:05.325 --> 00:21:06.666
I have friends.

00:21:06.726 --> 00:21:09.456
I like films, so I make films.

00:21:09.516 --> 00:21:10.886
I'm happy.

00:21:10.946 --> 00:21:12.946
What about you?

00:21:13.006 --> 00:21:15.126
I was happy.

00:21:15.186 --> 00:21:17.146
When I was an actress?

00:21:17.206 --> 00:21:18.217
There.

00:21:18.277 --> 00:21:19.617
There's your answer.

00:21:19.677 --> 00:21:21.468
Be an actress again.

00:21:21.528 --> 00:21:23.959
Jenny Lawson.

00:21:24.019 --> 00:21:25.379
Laura.

00:21:25.439 --> 00:21:27.760
What are you doing here?

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:29.850
Waiting for Gilbert.

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:31.661
And who is this?

00:21:31.721 --> 00:21:33.132
My name is Henry.

00:21:33.192 --> 00:21:34.552
I'm a film student.

00:21:34.612 --> 00:21:35.992
Sit down, Laura.

00:21:36.052 --> 00:21:36.803
Please.

00:21:36.863 --> 00:21:38.673
No, I can't stop.

00:21:38.733 --> 00:21:40.274
My children are here.

00:21:40.334 --> 00:21:42.514
We are all going to America.

00:21:42.574 --> 00:21:44.156
All the family.

00:21:44.216 --> 00:21:46.650
I write books now, you know.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.171
What do you do?

00:21:48.231 --> 00:21:49.241
Me?

00:21:49.302 --> 00:21:50.412
Nothing.

00:21:50.472 --> 00:21:51.774
Have you got children?

00:21:51.794 --> 00:21:53.104
No.

00:21:53.164 --> 00:21:55.626
You look unhappy, Jenny.

00:21:55.686 --> 00:21:59.660
At school, you were beautiful and good at everything.

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:04.284
And now you are older with no work and no children.

00:22:04.304 --> 00:22:06.666
Oh, dear.

00:22:06.726 --> 00:22:08.076
What?

00:22:08.136 --> 00:22:12.762
Laura, why did you say that?

00:22:12.822 --> 00:22:15.256
I have to go now.

00:22:15.316 --> 00:22:19.908
What's, what's that name on your bag?

00:22:19.968 --> 00:22:23.819
Henry Gilbert Lawson.

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.391
I know you now.

00:22:26.451 --> 00:22:32.064
Gilbert, you are Gilbert when he was 20 years old.

00:22:32.124 --> 00:22:34.125
But why are you here?

00:22:34.145 --> 00:22:40.882
Oh no!

00:22:40.942 --> 00:22:46.818
Scene three.

00:22:46.878 --> 00:22:49.440
Jenny learns about Gilbert.

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:52.010
There are four people at the check-in.

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:57.002
Woman one, woman two, a man, and Jenny's father.

00:22:57.062 --> 00:22:58.543
They're waiting.

00:22:58.603 --> 00:23:02.164
A British Airways man is looking at father's plane ticket.

00:23:02.224 --> 00:23:04.115
Jenny runs in.

00:23:04.175 --> 00:23:05.606
Excuse me.

00:23:05.626 --> 00:23:08.056
Oh, father.

00:23:08.116 --> 00:23:10.058
What are you doing here?

00:23:10.118 --> 00:23:12.058
Jenny, smile.

00:23:12.118 --> 00:23:13.369
Be happy.

00:23:13.429 --> 00:23:14.998
What?

00:23:15.058 --> 00:23:18.109
Hey, I was here before you.

00:23:18.129 --> 00:23:20.149
I was in front of you too.

00:23:20.209 --> 00:23:21.629
Are you okay, love?

00:23:21.689 --> 00:23:23.410
She's white in the face.

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:24.910
Excuse me.

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:26.691
Can you wait, please?

00:23:26.751 --> 00:23:27.751
No.

00:23:27.811 --> 00:23:30.062
My name is Jenny Lawson.

00:23:30.122 --> 00:23:32.682
Oh, Mrs Lawson.

00:23:32.742 --> 00:23:35.073
We phoned you at home.

00:23:35.133 --> 00:23:37.473
There was no answer.

00:23:37.533 --> 00:23:44.478
Mrs Lawson, I'm sorry, but Mr Lawson's plane crashed in the sea.

00:23:44.538 --> 00:23:46.712
He's dead.

00:23:46.772 --> 00:23:50.783
Oh, no!

00:23:50.843 --> 00:23:54.184
Scene four.

00:23:54.244 --> 00:23:56.994
Jenny understands everything.

00:23:57.054 --> 00:24:02.925
Jenny's father and mother and Jenny are all sitting at a table.

00:24:02.985 --> 00:24:06.266
They all died.

00:24:06.326 --> 00:24:08.796
All the people on the plane.

00:24:08.856 --> 00:24:10.856
Oh, Jenny.

00:24:10.916 --> 00:24:14.254
Your mother and I are so sorry, my love.

00:24:14.314 --> 00:24:15.822
Thank you.

00:24:15.882 --> 00:24:18.832
Why were you at the airport, Father?

00:24:18.892 --> 00:24:20.043
Me.

00:24:20.103 --> 00:24:22.003
I wasn't at the airport.

00:24:22.063 --> 00:24:23.504
Yes, you were.

00:24:23.564 --> 00:24:26.655
You were at the British Airways check-in desk.

00:24:26.715 --> 00:24:30.446
You said, be happy, then you left.

00:24:30.506 --> 00:24:31.726
No.

00:24:31.786 --> 00:24:35.088
Wait a minute.

00:24:35.148 --> 00:24:38.728
Hello, Laura.

00:24:38.788 --> 00:24:39.849
Laura.

00:24:39.909 --> 00:24:41.780
This is Jenny Lawson.

00:24:41.840 --> 00:24:43.857
We were at school together.

00:24:43.917 --> 00:24:47.707
Laura, I saw you at the airport, remember?

00:24:47.767 --> 00:24:49.148
And...

00:24:49.208 --> 00:24:50.970
Oh.

00:24:51.030 --> 00:24:53.612
What is Laura saying?

00:24:53.673 --> 00:24:57.236
She said, I wasn't at the airport.

00:24:57.296 --> 00:24:59.568
Laura, one question.

00:24:59.628 --> 00:25:02.220
Do you write books now?

00:25:02.280 --> 00:25:03.842
Yes.

00:25:03.902 --> 00:25:05.584
Thank you.

00:25:05.644 --> 00:25:08.076
She writes books.

00:25:08.136 --> 00:25:09.987
Is that important?

00:25:10.047 --> 00:25:10.964
Yes.

00:25:11.024 --> 00:25:15.122
Laura wants to write books, so she writes books.

00:25:15.182 --> 00:25:17.132
And she's happy.

00:25:17.192 --> 00:25:20.894
At the airport, father said, be happy.

00:25:20.954 --> 00:25:25.836
And Henry Gilbert Lawson said, be an actress again.

00:25:25.896 --> 00:25:28.416
I understand.

00:25:28.476 --> 00:25:31.168
I understand now too.

00:25:31.228 --> 00:25:36.150
My darling husband, I'm going to be an actress for you again.

00:25:36.170 --> 00:25:38.280
A good actress.

00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:39.928
Thank you.

00:25:39.988 --> 00:26:00.568
So sleep now, my darling.

00:26:00.628 --> 00:26:34.908
A Ghost in Love, performed by Jenny Bryce, Rupert Farley, Crispin Redmond, Patience Tomlinson.

00:26:34.969 --> 00:26:46.816
A Ghost in Love. Scene one.

00:26:46.876 --> 00:26:50.190
Brad sees a ghost.

00:26:50.250 --> 00:26:56.774
Brad and Jerry come into the hotel room and put their bags down.

00:26:56.834 --> 00:27:01.716
It is a hot day and they are wearing summer shirts.

00:27:01.776 --> 00:27:05.728
Brad sits on a bed.

00:27:05.788 --> 00:27:12.792
Man, we rode twenty miles in one morning.

00:27:12.852 --> 00:27:15.764
Are the bicycles okay in the street?

00:27:15.824 --> 00:27:17.734
In this little village?

00:27:17.794 --> 00:27:18.945
Oh, yes.

00:27:19.005 --> 00:27:21.587
Nobody steals bicycles here.

00:27:21.647 --> 00:27:22.968
How do you know?

00:27:22.988 --> 00:27:25.870
This is your first time here.

00:27:25.930 --> 00:27:27.952
First time in England.

00:27:28.012 --> 00:27:29.363
Or am I wrong?

00:27:29.423 --> 00:27:30.994
No, you're right.

00:27:31.054 --> 00:27:34.396
But I remember this village.

00:27:34.456 --> 00:27:36.708
I was here before, Jerry.

00:27:36.769 --> 00:27:38.310
I can feel it.

00:27:38.370 --> 00:27:40.612
Oh, come on.

00:27:40.672 --> 00:27:44.192
We were out in the sun for five hours.

00:27:44.252 --> 00:27:47.614
You need to drink some cold water, my friend.

00:27:47.673 --> 00:27:53.448
This hotel opened in 1853, right?

00:27:53.508 --> 00:27:56.100
Right.

00:27:56.160 --> 00:27:59.704
Brad, you looked at this book before.

00:27:59.764 --> 00:28:01.796
No, I didn't.

00:28:01.856 --> 00:28:04.888
Hey, you know something?

00:28:04.948 --> 00:28:07.030
It's 1:15.

00:28:07.090 --> 00:28:13.044
My dad died at this minute on this day, last month.

00:28:13.104 --> 00:28:15.803
Oh, Brad, I'm sorry.

00:28:15.863 --> 00:28:18.684
No, no, it's okay.

00:28:18.744 --> 00:28:25.346
I'm going to go back to New York next week after our three weeks in England.

00:28:25.406 --> 00:28:30.228
And I'm going to be Brad Davis of Davis TV.

00:28:30.288 --> 00:28:32.119
Dad wanted that.

00:28:32.179 --> 00:28:33.429
Yeah.

00:28:33.489 --> 00:28:35.840
Hey, come on.

00:28:35.900 --> 00:28:38.251
Let's go out in the sun.

00:28:38.311 --> 00:28:40.052
Let's see the village.

00:28:40.112 --> 00:28:41.352
Have a drink.

00:28:41.412 --> 00:28:42.993
Find some girls.

00:28:43.053 --> 00:28:44.724
No, you go.

00:28:44.784 --> 00:28:46.075
I like it here.

00:28:46.135 --> 00:28:48.096
Here in the room.

00:28:48.156 --> 00:28:51.728
Okay, let's stay in the room.

00:28:51.788 --> 00:28:55.772
Hey, there's a television.

00:28:55.832 --> 00:28:59.764
Hmm, not working.

00:28:59.824 --> 00:29:01.926
Oh, forget it.

00:29:01.986 --> 00:29:09.220
No, you're Brad Davis of Davis Television, the biggest in America.

00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:11.756
You must have a television.

00:29:11.816 --> 00:29:16.194
Look, shall I go down and ask Mrs. Finch?

00:29:16.254 --> 00:29:17.695
You stay here.

00:29:17.755 --> 00:29:19.286
You look tired.

00:29:19.346 --> 00:29:20.097
Yeah.

00:29:20.157 --> 00:29:21.408
Thanks, Jerry.

00:29:21.469 --> 00:29:26.263
I am tired.

00:29:26.323 --> 00:29:33.390
In 1760, the hotel was a house.

00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:37.580
A family called Banister lived in the house.

00:29:37.640 --> 00:29:42.040
One day, the 19-year-old daughter, Ellen.

00:29:42.100 --> 00:29:44.272
I was never 19.

00:29:44.332 --> 00:29:46.474
I died at 18.

00:29:46.534 --> 00:29:47.895
Yes.

00:29:47.956 --> 00:29:49.916
I remember you.

00:29:49.976 --> 00:29:51.458
Hello, Ellen.

00:29:51.518 --> 00:29:53.170
Hello, Matthew.

00:29:53.230 --> 00:29:56.332
Why does your friend call you Brad?

00:29:56.392 --> 00:29:57.943
Is that a name?

00:29:58.004 --> 00:29:59.074
Yes.

00:29:59.134 --> 00:30:01.316
It's an American name.

00:30:01.376 --> 00:30:03.148
But you are Matthew.

00:30:03.208 --> 00:30:05.960
And I'm going to call you Matthew.

00:30:06.020 --> 00:30:07.552
Always.

00:30:07.612 --> 00:30:13.254
Oh, Matthew, I waited and waited and waited for you.

00:30:13.314 --> 00:30:16.115
I love you so much.

00:30:16.175 --> 00:30:18.425
Do you love me?

00:30:18.486 --> 00:30:19.936
Yes.

00:30:19.996 --> 00:30:21.566
I think.

00:30:21.626 --> 00:30:23.777
Yes, I do.

00:30:23.837 --> 00:30:25.457
You think?

00:30:25.517 --> 00:30:27.438
Is that an answer?

00:30:27.498 --> 00:30:29.828
After all these years.

00:30:29.888 --> 00:30:31.519
Oh, Matthew.

00:30:31.579 --> 00:30:34.630
Matthew, do you remember everything?

00:30:34.690 --> 00:30:37.358
No, not everything.

00:30:37.418 --> 00:30:41.347
I remember our love, and you died.

00:30:41.407 --> 00:30:43.008
I remember that.

00:30:43.068 --> 00:30:45.279
I wanted to die, too.

00:30:45.339 --> 00:30:49.401
And again, last month, I wanted to die.

00:30:49.461 --> 00:30:52.592
Oh, Matthew, don't say that.

00:30:52.652 --> 00:30:57.255
Oh, Matthew, I'm so happy to see you again.

00:30:57.315 --> 00:31:00.286
Ellen, can I see you?

00:31:00.346 --> 00:31:01.888
Can we talk?

00:31:01.948 --> 00:31:03.478
Oh, yes.

00:31:03.538 --> 00:31:05.449
I want to talk to you about...

00:31:05.509 --> 00:31:06.918
Are you okay, love?

00:31:06.978 --> 00:31:08.836
You look white.

00:31:08.896 --> 00:31:11.967
This is not a happy time for Brad.

00:31:12.027 --> 00:31:13.757
I'm sorry love.

00:31:13.817 --> 00:31:15.868
Do you want some dinner?

00:31:15.928 --> 00:31:19.859
I make the best dinner in the north of England.

00:31:19.919 --> 00:31:20.800
No.

00:31:20.860 --> 00:31:22.010
Thank you.

00:31:22.070 --> 00:31:24.141
Talk to me later then.

00:31:24.201 --> 00:31:25.271
Right.

00:31:25.331 --> 00:31:27.872
The television.

00:31:27.932 --> 00:31:30.363
It's okay now.

00:31:30.383 --> 00:31:32.494
Bye bye Brad.

00:31:32.554 --> 00:31:33.884
Bye Jerry.

00:31:33.944 --> 00:31:36.606
Have a nice time in our village.

00:31:36.666 --> 00:31:40.550
Mrs. Finch, wait, please.

00:31:40.610 --> 00:31:43.912
Do you know about the Banister family?

00:31:43.972 --> 00:31:46.303
Did you see the ghost?

00:31:46.363 --> 00:31:48.164
Ellen Banister?

00:31:48.224 --> 00:31:49.395
Yes.

00:31:49.455 --> 00:31:50.716
What?

00:31:50.776 --> 00:31:52.076
Brad?

00:31:52.136 --> 00:31:53.978
You saw a ghost?

00:31:54.038 --> 00:31:55.829
Oh, come on.

00:31:55.889 --> 00:31:58.551
Oh, Ellen's always here.

00:31:58.611 --> 00:32:00.822
She likes young men.

00:32:00.882 --> 00:32:04.304
She's always looking for her boyfriend.

00:32:04.365 --> 00:32:07.077
Matthew's his name, I think.

00:32:07.138 --> 00:32:09.890
Mrs. Finch, what happened?

00:32:09.950 --> 00:32:11.690
How did she die?

00:32:11.750 --> 00:32:14.121
What happened to Matthew?

00:32:14.181 --> 00:32:16.122
You're interested, love.

00:32:16.182 --> 00:32:18.192
I can see that.

00:32:18.252 --> 00:32:21.144
There's an old woman in the village.

00:32:21.204 --> 00:32:23.784
Her name is Maud Anscombe.

00:32:23.844 --> 00:32:25.885
She knows about Ellen.

00:32:25.945 --> 00:32:28.636
You ask Maud.

00:32:28.696 --> 00:32:32.327
Brad, this ghost.

00:32:32.387 --> 00:32:34.278
What did she say?

00:32:34.338 --> 00:32:35.638
She...

00:32:35.698 --> 00:32:37.491
She didn't speak.

00:32:37.551 --> 00:32:38.424
Jerry.

00:32:38.484 --> 00:32:43.056
She said nothing at all.

00:32:43.116 --> 00:32:46.658
Scene two.

00:32:46.718 --> 00:32:51.682
Brad and Jerry want to know about Ellen.

00:32:51.742 --> 00:32:55.744
Maud is a very old woman.

00:32:55.804 --> 00:32:58.044
Her hair is white.

00:32:58.104 --> 00:33:04.656
Brad and Jerry are sitting at a table with her in her house.

00:33:04.716 --> 00:33:08.037
A little banister.

00:33:08.057 --> 00:33:12.430
A bad, bad girl.

00:33:12.490 --> 00:33:19.596
When she looked at someone, the next day they were ill.

00:33:19.656 --> 00:33:22.338
So she was a witch?

00:33:22.398 --> 00:33:23.708
Yes.

00:33:23.768 --> 00:33:27.162
She looked at animals too.

00:33:27.222 --> 00:33:34.342
Then all the cows in the village had no milk in them.

00:33:34.402 --> 00:33:37.038
Do you know this?

00:33:37.098 --> 00:33:38.799
How do you know?

00:33:38.859 --> 00:33:40.809
How can you know?

00:33:40.829 --> 00:33:45.660
Oh, it's in all the books.

00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:54.132
Our village is famous because of bad Ellen Banister.

00:33:54.192 --> 00:33:58.103
Scene three.

00:33:58.163 --> 00:34:01.414
Was Ellen a witch?

00:34:01.474 --> 00:34:04.074
Brad and Jerry?

00:34:04.134 --> 00:34:07.134
Are in Mrs. Morgan's village shop.

00:34:07.194 --> 00:34:11.746
There are two men and three women in the shop.

00:34:11.806 --> 00:34:14.246
And Mrs. Morgan.

00:34:14.307 --> 00:34:15.967
Yes?

00:34:16.027 --> 00:34:17.578
Are you next?

00:34:17.638 --> 00:34:18.888
Yes.

00:34:18.948 --> 00:34:20.929
Two cokes, please.

00:34:20.989 --> 00:34:23.290
And two of those sandwiches?

00:34:23.350 --> 00:34:25.030
I'm not hungry.

00:34:25.090 --> 00:34:27.891
Man, you must eat.

00:34:27.952 --> 00:34:32.506
You can't sit in your room all day and wait for a ghost.

00:34:32.566 --> 00:34:35.742
That's six pounds, please.

00:34:35.803 --> 00:34:38.084
Who was this?

00:34:38.144 --> 00:34:39.676
Ellen Banister?

00:34:39.736 --> 00:34:40.907
Yes.

00:34:40.968 --> 00:34:43.990
Do you know about Ellen Banister?

00:34:44.050 --> 00:34:48.054
Oh, people in our village had no money then.

00:34:48.114 --> 00:34:50.715
Of course they stole things.

00:34:50.776 --> 00:34:53.648
And Ellen Banister sold them.

00:34:53.709 --> 00:34:56.191
She only wanted to help.

00:34:56.250 --> 00:34:58.472
Was she a witch?

00:34:58.533 --> 00:35:00.384
Some people say that.

00:35:00.444 --> 00:35:02.176
A witch?

00:35:02.236 --> 00:35:05.448
No, of course not.

00:35:05.508 --> 00:35:07.610
The men loved her.

00:35:07.670 --> 00:35:09.851
She helped them, you see.

00:35:09.912 --> 00:35:15.265
Though women didn't love her so much, she was beautiful, you see.

00:35:15.325 --> 00:35:19.708
Her boyfriend was the bad one, that Matthew.

00:35:19.768 --> 00:35:22.020
It wasn't her.

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:25.592
Oh, what did he do?

00:35:25.652 --> 00:35:29.785
He stole things from rich people.

00:35:29.845 --> 00:35:35.206
Then she sold them, and he took all the money.

00:35:35.266 --> 00:35:38.197
He took all her money, too.

00:35:38.258 --> 00:35:40.128
But she loved him.

00:35:40.188 --> 00:35:42.189
Did he love her?

00:35:42.249 --> 00:35:43.349
No.

00:35:43.409 --> 00:35:45.630
He had two or three women.

00:35:45.690 --> 00:35:47.871
No, he didn't.

00:35:47.931 --> 00:35:49.541
He loved her.

00:35:49.601 --> 00:35:51.202
He lived for her.

00:35:51.222 --> 00:35:53.292
Who are you talking about?

00:35:53.352 --> 00:35:55.420
That witch Ellen Banister?

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:57.998
She ate cats for breakfast.

00:35:58.058 --> 00:35:58.768
No!

00:35:58.828 --> 00:36:01.330
Don't listen to him!

00:36:01.390 --> 00:36:05.111
Don't listen to these people, you boys.

00:36:05.171 --> 00:36:07.972
What happened to Ellen Banister?

00:36:08.032 --> 00:36:10.373
You want to know that?

00:36:10.433 --> 00:36:14.774
Matthew killed her.

00:36:14.835 --> 00:36:18.426
Scene four.

00:36:18.486 --> 00:36:21.358
Where is Ellen now?

00:36:21.418 --> 00:36:23.527
It is nighttime.

00:36:23.587 --> 00:36:26.777
Jerry is sitting on the bed.

00:36:26.837 --> 00:36:31.859
Brad is walking up and down.

00:36:31.919 --> 00:36:35.530
Seven hours.

00:36:35.591 --> 00:36:38.582
We waited seven hours.

00:36:38.642 --> 00:36:40.742
Where is she, Jerry?

00:36:40.802 --> 00:36:42.883
I said this before.

00:36:42.943 --> 00:36:44.564
I don't know.

00:36:44.624 --> 00:36:46.044
Just wait.

00:36:46.104 --> 00:36:50.356
She isn't coming because you're here.

00:36:50.416 --> 00:36:53.364
Brad, I say again.

00:36:53.424 --> 00:36:56.103
One, I sleep here.

00:36:56.163 --> 00:36:58.103
This is my room.

00:36:58.164 --> 00:37:04.766
Two, I am your friend, and I am not leaving you like this.

00:37:04.826 --> 00:37:09.578
Jerry, is this all a big laugh for you?

00:37:09.638 --> 00:37:12.508
No, not now.

00:37:12.569 --> 00:37:15.120
I want to see Ellen too.

00:37:15.180 --> 00:37:16.840
I want to help.

00:37:16.900 --> 00:37:18.260
Okay.

00:37:18.321 --> 00:37:20.301
Thanks, Jerry.

00:37:20.361 --> 00:37:21.512
Sorry.

00:37:21.572 --> 00:37:22.702
Hey!

00:37:22.763 --> 00:37:24.974
Here she is.

00:37:25.034 --> 00:37:26.634
Ellen.

00:37:26.694 --> 00:37:28.035
Ellen.

00:37:28.095 --> 00:37:29.475
It's me.

00:37:29.535 --> 00:37:30.946
Brad.

00:37:31.006 --> 00:37:32.656
Matthew.

00:37:32.716 --> 00:37:34.027
Man.

00:37:34.087 --> 00:37:35.328
Oh man.

00:37:35.388 --> 00:37:37.118
It's all true.

00:37:37.178 --> 00:37:38.238
Ellen.

00:37:38.298 --> 00:37:39.639
Please.

00:37:39.699 --> 00:37:41.120
Tell me.

00:37:41.180 --> 00:37:44.351
What happened in 1760?

00:37:44.411 --> 00:37:46.491
You must remember.

00:37:46.552 --> 00:37:47.802
No.

00:37:47.862 --> 00:37:49.833
We sold things.

00:37:49.893 --> 00:37:51.121
You and me.

00:37:51.182 --> 00:37:53.400
Rich people's things.

00:37:53.460 --> 00:37:56.021
You stole them, remember?

00:37:56.081 --> 00:37:57.702
Wow.

00:37:57.762 --> 00:38:01.122
Brad, you were Robin Hood.

00:38:01.182 --> 00:38:02.573
Sorry.

00:38:02.633 --> 00:38:05.704
The rich people didn't like me.

00:38:05.764 --> 00:38:08.775
They said bad things about me.

00:38:08.835 --> 00:38:11.956
Ellen Banister is a witch.

00:38:12.016 --> 00:38:15.726
They said that, but it's not true.

00:38:15.786 --> 00:38:17.417
Of course not.

00:38:17.477 --> 00:38:21.240
Then, one day, they came for us.

00:38:21.300 --> 00:38:23.022
Twenty men.

00:38:23.082 --> 00:38:24.543
What happened?

00:38:24.603 --> 00:38:26.383
We ran away.

00:38:26.443 --> 00:38:28.544
You found a ship.

00:38:28.604 --> 00:38:31.474
A ship going to America.

00:38:31.534 --> 00:38:37.155
You said, see you at one fifteen at the harbor.

00:38:37.215 --> 00:38:38.966
We can go away.

00:38:39.026 --> 00:38:40.726
You and me.

00:38:40.786 --> 00:38:43.466
And then what happened, Ellen?

00:38:43.526 --> 00:38:46.277
The ship went early.

00:38:46.337 --> 00:38:48.507
I wasn't there in time.

00:38:48.527 --> 00:38:51.304
You went on the ship.

00:38:51.364 --> 00:38:53.771
You didn't wait for me.

00:38:53.831 --> 00:38:55.371
Oh, no.

00:38:55.432 --> 00:39:00.174
When I arrived, there were a lot of ships there.

00:39:00.234 --> 00:39:03.775
I didn't know the name of our ship.

00:39:03.836 --> 00:39:05.656
I looked for you.

00:39:05.716 --> 00:39:09.998
I waited and waited and waited.

00:39:10.058 --> 00:39:11.099
Ellen.

00:39:11.159 --> 00:39:14.090
Oh, Ellen, I'm sorry.

00:39:14.150 --> 00:39:16.361
Then the men came.

00:39:16.421 --> 00:39:18.992
They put me in prison.

00:39:19.053 --> 00:39:20.616
I died.

00:39:20.676 --> 00:39:22.972
Three months later.

00:39:23.032 --> 00:39:25.914
And then I came back home.

00:39:25.975 --> 00:39:27.326
Here.

00:39:27.386 --> 00:39:29.708
And I waited again.

00:39:29.768 --> 00:39:31.489
I waited for you.

00:39:31.509 --> 00:39:34.311
I love you, Ellen.

00:39:34.371 --> 00:39:39.415
I love you too, Matthew.

00:39:39.475 --> 00:39:43.438
Scene five.

00:39:43.498 --> 00:39:46.081
What is Brad going to do?

00:39:46.101 --> 00:39:48.961
It is dark.

00:39:49.021 --> 00:39:52.730
Brad is standing at the window of the room.

00:39:52.790 --> 00:39:54.951
Jerry comes in.

00:39:55.011 --> 00:40:00.614
Brad always has his back to Jerry in this scene.

00:40:00.674 --> 00:40:03.744
Do you want to die?

00:40:03.804 --> 00:40:06.495
Do you want to go to Ellen?

00:40:06.555 --> 00:40:10.767
Before today, the answer was yes.

00:40:10.827 --> 00:40:15.599
Matthew wanted to die and go to be with Ellen.

00:40:15.659 --> 00:40:17.960
Do you understand that?

00:40:18.020 --> 00:40:19.157
Yes.

00:40:19.217 --> 00:40:24.158
But Matthew is dead, and I am Brad now.

00:40:24.218 --> 00:40:27.320
And what does Brad want?

00:40:27.380 --> 00:40:29.322
I don't know.

00:40:29.382 --> 00:40:31.163
I'm thinking.

00:40:31.224 --> 00:40:34.946
Is there a train from here to London tomorrow?

00:40:35.006 --> 00:40:36.268
Yes.

00:40:36.328 --> 00:40:40.160
We can put our bicycles on the train.

00:40:40.220 --> 00:40:44.174
We can get the next plane back to America.

00:40:44.234 --> 00:40:46.726
Do you want to do that?

00:40:46.786 --> 00:40:48.412
I don't know.

00:40:48.472 --> 00:40:52.711
I'm going to tell you tomorrow.

00:40:52.771 --> 00:40:55.784
Scene six.

00:40:55.844 --> 00:40:58.946
In love with a ghost.

00:40:59.006 --> 00:41:01.128
The next day.

00:41:01.188 --> 00:41:04.801
Brad and Jerry are in the street.

00:41:04.861 --> 00:41:07.794
Jerry has two bags.

00:41:07.854 --> 00:41:11.216
Mrs Finch is there too.

00:41:11.276 --> 00:41:13.678
You must leave then.

00:41:13.698 --> 00:41:15.720
A week early.

00:41:15.780 --> 00:41:18.447
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:41:18.507 --> 00:41:20.122
Oh, hello.

00:41:20.182 --> 00:41:22.164
It's the American boys.

00:41:22.224 --> 00:41:24.324
Are you going home to America?

00:41:24.384 --> 00:41:27.286
Jerry's going home, Mrs. Morgan.

00:41:27.346 --> 00:41:30.717
I'm staying here at the hotel.

00:41:30.777 --> 00:41:32.868
I'm going to live here.

00:41:32.928 --> 00:41:34.358
Always.

00:41:34.418 --> 00:41:38.160
Brad, do you want to do this?

00:41:38.220 --> 00:41:41.281
Think about Davis TV.

00:41:41.341 --> 00:41:44.802
What are you going to do here in England?

00:41:44.862 --> 00:41:46.292
I don't know.

00:41:46.352 --> 00:41:51.142
But yes, Davis TV needs a good man.

00:41:51.203 --> 00:41:55.466
My dad worked for years for Davis TV.

00:41:55.526 --> 00:41:59.368
But now it has a good man, Jerry.

00:41:59.428 --> 00:42:00.558
You.

00:42:00.618 --> 00:42:02.090
Me?

00:42:02.150 --> 00:42:05.221
Oh, thank you, Brad.

00:42:05.281 --> 00:42:07.272
That's okay.

00:42:07.332 --> 00:42:08.994
I'm happy.

00:42:09.054 --> 00:42:11.014
I'm in love.

00:42:11.074 --> 00:42:15.336
She waited for me, and now I'm here.

00:42:15.397 --> 00:42:18.757
I am never going to leave her again.